{"id":"771a3bc06fe844ae8a317c0b7bf4a5d234a77dca","axis":"silent","repo":"microsoft/vscode","sha":"771a3bc06fe844ae8a317c0b7bf4a5d234a77dca","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"src/vs/sessions/AUTOMATIONS.md","lines":["@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@ Agent Host Cron schedules use the existing five-field [AHP grammar](../platform/"," "," The Agent Host adapter persists an explicitly chosen CRON editing form in definition metadata without changing trigger semantics. Definitions without this preference keep their existing preset projection."," ","-Cloud ownership is separate from the execution target and creator: `user` (Only me) or `repository`, defaulting to `user` for legacy responses. Ownership is accepted only on creation, never in updates. The create API is authoritative for repository ownership support, and providers translate its known unsupported-ownership rejection into product-facing feedback. The repository Automation capability must allow management for cloud mutations. Providers project whether the signed-in user created a definition independently of management permissions. The Automations view applies the user's shared-creator visibility preference consistently to cards, run history, bulk mark-read, and accessible content. The cloud provider skips history requests for hidden definitions and excludes their cached runs from its published run list, including sidebar attention indicators. Preference changes refresh history; in-flight responses cannot republish hidden runs. The complete definition catalogue remains available to agent tools and visibility discovery, and filtering never changes execution or authorization.","+Cloud ownership is separate from the execution target and creator: `user` (Only me) or `repository`, defaulting to `user` for legacy responses. Ownership is accepted only on creation, never in updates. The create API is authoritative for repository ownership support, and providers translate its known unsupported-ownership rejection into product-facing feedback. The repository Automation capability must allow management for cloud mutations. Providers project whether the signed-in user created a definition independently of management permissions. The Automations view applies the user's shared-creator visibility preference consistently to cards, run history, bulk mark-read, and accessible content. This preference is machine-local profile UI state, shared by the cards and modal menus, not a configuration setting. The cloud provider skips history requests for hidden definitions and excludes their cached runs from its published run list, including sidebar attention indicators. Preference changes refresh history; in-flight responses cannot republish hidden runs. The complete definition catalogue remains available to agent tools and visibility discovery, and filtering never changes execution or authorization."," "," An `AutomationTarget` separates concrete provider identity (`providerId`) from its agent (`sessionTypeId`). Workspace targets also carry the workspace URI and isolation choice. Session type or display name alone cannot determine ownership. Creation requires an explicit, available Automation-capable provider."," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/vs/sessions/common/agentsWindowContextKeys.ts","lines":["@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ export const CustomViewVisibleContext = new RawContextKey<boolean>('customViewVi"," export const AutomationsCustomViewFocusContext = new RawContextKey<boolean>('automationsCustomViewFocus', false, localize('automationsCustomViewFocus', \"Whether the Automations custom view has keyboard focus\"));"," export const AutomationsHasItemsContext = new RawContextKey<boolean>('automationsHasItems', false, localize('automationsHasItems', \"Whether there is at least one automation\"));"," export const AutomationsHasOthersContext = new RawContextKey<boolean>('automationsHasOthers', false, localize('automationsHasOthers', \"Whether there is a shared automation not known to be created by the